meta {
  name: Upload Rewrite Document
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{rewriteDocumentUploadUrl}}
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/pdf
}

body:text {
  %PDF-1.4
  1 0 obj<</Type/Catalog>>endobj
  trailer<</Root 1 0 R>>
  %%EOF
}

tests {
  test("storage accepts the application", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  # PUT <uploadUrl> — the raw rewrite document upload

  Not an API endpoint: this goes **straight to object storage** using the URL
  from `Presign Rewrite Document`.

  - **Auth:** `none` — deliberately. The collection-level bearer would be sent on
    this request and **break the S3 signature**; a presigned URL carries its own
    credentials.

  ## Headers
  `Content-Type` must be `application/pdf` — it has to match the signed value,
  and the application kind accepts nothing else.

  ## Body
  A minimal valid PDF stub. The bytes are irrelevant to the API; only the
  object's type and size matter, and `POST /policies/:id/rewrite` reads both back
  with `HeadObject` rather than trusting anything declared.

  ## Run order
  Must run **between** `Presign Rewrite Document` (seq 3) and `Rewrite Policy`
  (seq 5): the object has to exist before the rewrite declares its key, because
  `verifyAttachments` does a real `HeadObject` and a missing object is a 400.
}
